Subject: [PATCH 10/17] ttf: state GDEF's glyph classes in the features

A compiler derives GDEF glyph classes from glyph categories and anchors, and
writes no GDEF at all when no glyph is a mark, a ligature or an anchored base.
A font whose GDEF calls its combining accents bases (they space, and no
lookup attaches them) then built with no GDEF, and a shaper took the accents
for marks again by their codepoints.

The glyph classes are now written as a GlyphClassDef statement, as the
lookups already are, with glyph names that are feature-file keywords escaped.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
